schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: US crypto-related losses reported to the FBI hit $9.3B in 2024
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Victims reported $9.3 billion in crypto-related losses to the FBI in
    2024, a 66% jump from the year before; investment fraud was the single
    largest category at $5.8 billion.
  evidence: 'FBI 2024 Internet Crime Report (IC3), cited by URL in the article''s references.'
  source_lineage: 'FBI 2024 Internet Crime Report (IC3) — https://www.ic3.gov/AnnualReport/Reports/2024_IC3Report.pdf'
  interpretation: >-
    Used to establish stakes before walking through specific scam types;
    investment-fraud share motivates the article's dedicated "too-good-to-be-
    true returns" section.
  uncertainty: >-
    FBI IC3 figures rely on victim self-reporting, which undercounts actual
    losses (many victims don't report). Not independently re-verified against
    the source PDF here.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/common-scams.md
    transformation: quoted
    authorship: ai-assisted
